        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nPAUL D. POLIDORO, ESQ., Patterson, New York; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nABRAHAM CANTOR, ESQ., Concord, Ohio; on behalf of the Respondents.\nDAVID M. GORMLEY, ESQ., Solicitor General, Columbus, Ohio; on behalf of Ohio, et al., as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a criminal act to go from door to door in the Village of Stratton and deliver that message unless one has first obtained a permit from the village to do so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But you emphasize only the latter, really, in your briefs. Are the records that the mayor keeps, are they open to the public?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Polidoro (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice O'Connor, my experience is quite to the opposite, that after the battles between Jehovah's Witnesses and the municipalities in the thirties and forties, municipalities have stopped attempting to regulate Jehovah's Witnesses by forcing them to get a permit to go from door to door."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But suppose I am concerned that the mayor, in my view, or the Government has no right to demand previous registration or to give his consent before I go to my neighbors to talk about neighborhood problems, or whatever."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that your objection, that you do not want to have to go to city hall in order to ring doorbells --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cantor (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1737",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "59d8591f9a3dc92d965e0c54afa094ac5a2d844c2e761a81a4cb95aeae6eb7b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-59d8591f9a3d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The city's purpose is to prevent annoyance of the property owner."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
